%N A400354 Column of the rightmost maximum entry in the n-th row of A032531.
%C A400354 It appears that this sequence exhibits an overall tendency to increase, although this is not yet proven and it decreases at certain indices. The plateau of A401242 from n=2137 to 7078 is depicted within this sequence at a(n)=16 for n=2137 to 7078 and a(7079)=370. This sequence is closely related to A401242, and the two sequences are indexed identically. It is yet unproven that the sequence tends to infinity, stabilizes at a constant, or exhibits any other type of asymptotic behavior. By definition, the sequence is infinite and consists of nonnegative integers satisfying 0 <= a(n) <= n.
%H A400354 Yifeng Zou, <a href="/A400354/b400354.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%e A400354 For n=3, a(3)=1, as row 3 of A032531 consists of 2,3,1,2, of which the maximum value is located in column 1.
%o A400354 (Python)
%o A400354 from collections import Counter
%o A400354 def rightmost_max_index_A032531(n):
%o A400354     counts = Counter()
%o A400354     result = []
%o A400354     for row in range(n + 1):
%o A400354         maximum = -1
%o A400354         rightmost_index = 0
%o A400354         for k in range(row + 1):
%o A400354             value = counts[k]
%o A400354             if value >= maximum:
%o A400354                 maximum = value
%o A400354                 rightmost_index = k
%o A400354             counts[value] += 1
%o A400354         result.append(rightmost_index)
%o A400354     return result
%o A400354 print(rightmost_max_index_A032531(86))
%Y A400354 Cf. A401242, A032531.
%K A400354 nonn,new
